{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אני אל שדי פרה ורבה", :translit "ani el shaddai p'reh u-r'vah", :gloss "I am El Shaddai, be fruitful and multiply"} {:he "שי״ן דל״ת יו״ד", :translit "shin dalet yod", :gloss "shin dalet yod"} {:he "ת״ק", :translit "tak", :gloss "500"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Hidden (standard) spelling of ש-ד-י expanded as שין דלת יוד; the openly written letters ש-ד-י = 314 are subtracted from the full expansion total, leaving the hidden letters."} {:kind :gematria, :a "שי״ן דל״ת יו״ד", :b "ת״ק"}], :frame {:text "The name שדי (El Shaddai) is connected to fertility: God says 'I am El Shaddai, be fruitful and multiply' to Jacob in Genesis 35:11, and the same name appears with the command 'be fruitful and multiply' to Abraham in Genesis 17:1–2. The expansion of the divine name שדי by inserting the standard orthographic fill letters (שין-דלת-יוד) is a standard technique of gematria on divine names. The number 500 corresponds to the tally of limbs in the human body as recorded in the Mishnah, which counts 248 limbs in a man and 252 in a woman (Mishnah Oholot 1:8).", :sources ["Genesis 35:11" "Genesis 17:1" "Mishnah Oholot 1:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "גוי וקהל גוים יהיה ממך", :translit "goy u-k'hal goyim yihyeh mi-mekha", :gloss "a nation and a congregation of nations shall be from you"} {:he "ירבעם", :translit "yarav'am", :gloss "Jeroboam"} {:he "יהוא", :translit "yehu", :gloss "Jehu"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "גוי וקהל גוים יהיה ממך", :b "ירבעם ויהוא"}], :frame {:text "The verse 'a nation and a congregation of nations shall be from you' was spoken to Jacob at Bethel (Genesis 35:11). Jeroboam son of Nebat led the northern kingdom of Israel into sin after the monarchy split (1 Kings 12:26–30), and Jehu was anointed king of Israel and exterminated the house of Ahab (2 Kings 9–10). Both were Israelite monarchs descended from Jacob.", :sources ["Genesis 35:11" "1 Kings 12:26" "2 Kings 9:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Hidden (standard) spelling of ש-ד-י expanded as שין דלת יוד; the openly written letters ש-ד-י = 314 are subtracted from the full expansion total, leaving the hidden letters.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "שי״ן דל״ת יו״ד", :a-value 814, :b "ת״ק", :b-value 500, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:a-value 349, :b-value 350, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "ירבעם ויהוא", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "גוי וקהל גוים יהיה ממך"}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:08.605396747Z", :model "glm-5.2"}